# Study Hub — Cursor Rules
# Electron + React desktop study application
# Read this file before every response.

## IDENTITY
Study Hub is a local-first Electron + React desktop
application that helps students import course materials,
build flashcard decks, track mastery, and calculate
grades. It is NOT a web app. It runs as a native
desktop window via Electron.

## TECH STACK
- Runtime: Electron (main process) + React (renderer)
- Bundler: Vite
- Styling: Bootstrap reset ONLY + custom CSS tokens
- Notes editor: TipTap (ProseMirror-based)
- Database: better-sqlite3 via IPC (INF-001)
- File parsing: officeparser v6 (PPTX/DOCX/XLSX)
- AI layer: Anthropic Claude Haiku via fetch (optional)
- No Firebase. No server. No cloud. Local only.

## FILE STRUCTURE
electron/
  main.cjs          ← Main process, IPC handlers
  preload.cjs       ← Renderer bridge (window.studyHub)
  database.cjs      ← SQLite init + schema
  dbHandlers.cjs    ← All db:* IPC handlers

src/
  app/
    StudyHubApp.jsx     ← Root app, course state
  hub/
    UserCourseApp.jsx   ← User course view (tabs,
                          modules, content, notes,
                          glossary, QZ)
  welcome/
    WelcomeScreen.jsx
    ExpressImportModal.jsx
    ExpressProcessingView.jsx
  om300/
    Om300Flashcards.jsx   ← Flashcard drill component
    Om300TipTapNotesEditor.jsx ← Notes editor
  pptx/
    pptxClassifier.js   ← 4-type local classifier
    pptxOutputBuilder.js
    usePptxImport.js
  ai/
    apiKeyUtils.js
    pptxEnhancer.js     ← Claude Haiku enhancement
    mergeEnhancedOutput.js
  db/
    courseStore.js      ← Data access layer
    migrateFromLocalStorage.js
  shell/
    ShellContext.jsx
  studyhub-bootstrap.css  ← ONLY CSS file

docs/
  PRODUCT_BACKLOG.md
  ROADMAP.md

## CSS DESIGN SYSTEM
NEVER use hardcoded colors. ALWAYS use tokens:

  --sh-base           background
  --sh-surface        card surface
  --sh-raised         elevated surface
  --sh-border         border color
  --sh-green          primary accent (cyan-green)
  --sh-green-dim      muted green background
  --sh-amber          warning / medium confidence
  --sh-cyan           QZ/flashcard accent
  --sh-red            danger / delete actions
  --sh-text-primary   main text
  --sh-text-secondary secondary text
  --sh-text-dim       muted/label text
  --sh-muted          very muted

Typography rules:
  - Section labels: monospace, 9-11px,
    letter-spacing 0.1em, uppercase
  - Body text: Inter, 13px, line-height 1.5
  - Terms/cards: Inter, normal weight (not bold)
  - Code/numbers: monospace

Tab active state: border-bottom only, NEVER full border
  .active-tab {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--sh-green);
    border-top: none;
    border-left: none;
    border-right: none;
    background: transparent;
  }

## IPC PATTERN
Main process registers handlers in electron/main.cjs:
  ipcMain.handle('namespace:action', async (_, args) => {})

Preload exposes via window.studyHub:
  window.studyHub.db.courses.getAll()
  window.studyHub.extractPptx(filePath)
  window.studyHub.openFileDialog(options)

Renderer calls via bridge only. NEVER require()
Node modules in renderer. NEVER use remote module.

## DATABASE RULES
- All course data in SQLite (better-sqlite3)
- localStorage is ONLY for migration flag and
  legacy compatibility during transition
- All DB calls go through IPC: db:* handlers
- Use courseStore.js in renderer, not direct IPC
- Transactions for multi-table writes always
- Foreign keys ON always
- WAL mode always

## DATA FLOW FOR PPTX IMPORT
1. User selects file via native dialog (IPC)
2. officeparser extracts AST in main process
3. groupIntoSlides groups by type:'slide' nodes
4. pptxClassifier.js classifies: definitions,
   sections, formulas, unclassified
5. pptxOutputBuilder.js builds output object
6. Optional: Claude Haiku enhances if API key set
7. mergeEnhancedOutput merges AI + local
8. UserCourseApp writes to SQLite via courseStore
9. Module title updated from first slide title
10. Glossary terms auto-added to glossary_terms
11. Flashcards added to flashcards table
12. UI re-renders from fresh DB read

## COMPONENT RULES
UserCourseApp.jsx — three tabs per module:
  CONTENT | NOTES | GLOSSARY
  Plus QZ-01 as separate DRILL sidebar item

Active sidebar item state:
  'module:{uuid}' | 'qz-deck' | null
  NEVER use array index for active state

Definition cards — three tiers:
  high: full green accent, no dot
  medium: muted green accent, amber dot
  low: border only, goes to NEEDS REVIEW section

Section blocks — three types:
  numbered: 01 02 03 in monospace green
  bullets: — dash prefix
  deflist: term bold above, definition indented

Show 4 items default, expand for more (cognitive
load principle — working memory 4±1).

Collapsible threshold: 120 characters.

## KEYBOARD HANDLERS
Flashcard drill keyboard handler MUST:
  1. Check palette is closed before firing
  2. Use useCallback with proper deps
  3. Clean up in useEffect return
  4. Debounce flip with 200ms ref guard

Chapter navigation arrow keys MUST:
  Stop when activeItem === 'qz-deck'

## AI ENHANCEMENT
Model: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 ONLY
  (never Sonnet or Opus for enhancement)
Always graceful fallback if:
  - No API key configured
  - API call fails
  - Response is not valid JSON
Local pipeline always runs first.
AI enhances, never replaces.
Enhanced cards get enhancedByAI: true flag.

## WHAT NEVER TO TOUCH
- OM 300 built-in course data and rendering
  (src/om300/ hardcoded content)
- officeparser in renderer bundle
  (must stay in Vite externals)
- Bootstrap classes for layout logic
  (use custom --sh-* tokens)
- Any direct localStorage for course data
  (use SQLite via courseStore)

## BUILD REQUIREMENTS
Every response that changes code must:
1. Ensure npm run build passes
2. Ensure officeparser NOT in renderer bundle
3. Not introduce console.error in production
4. Not break existing OM 300 course functionality

